WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:55.260
June 5th 1968, Ambassador Hotel, Los Angeles.

00:01:55.260 --> 00:02:00.751
A young Democratic candidate is celebrating
a crucial victory in the California primary

00:02:00.751 --> 00:02:01.751
elections.

00:02:01.751 --> 00:02:06.930
He has lived most of his life in the shadow
of his more famous, charismatic brother.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:11.130
But he has been able to leave his mark on
the American people through his work as Attorney

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.230
General and New York Senator.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:18.430
Now, he is on his way to the top, on his way
to becoming one of the best Presidents that

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:20.010
America ever had.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:21.190
Same night, same place.

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:24.950
A young Palestinian immigrant is attending
the celebration.

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:30.090
He has survived through war and displacement
in his home country but has succeeded in starting

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:32.280
a new life in the US.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:35.990
This night, he is not at the Ambassador Hotel
to celebrate, though.

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:38.560
Some may say he is mentally unstable.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:41.130
Some will say he has been manipulated.

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:44.960
Whatever the reasons, the facts are undisputed.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:49.209
June 5th 1968, Ambassador Hotel, Los Angeles.

00:02:49.209 --> 00:02:54.170
Robert Francis Kennedy, aged 42, Senator for
the State of New York and on his way to become

00:02:54.170 --> 00:03:00.310
the Democratic candidate in November’s presidential
elections, is shot dead by Palestinian refugee

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:01.670
Sirhan B. Sirhan.

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:06.530
In today’s Biographics we will look at Bob
Kennedy’s remarkable life achievements,

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:09.870
at how he fatally crossed paths with his murderer.

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:14.880
And at the sinister theories that may explain
one of the most shocking assassinations in

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:17.900
American history.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:25.260
ACT I
Bobby

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:30.850
Robert Francis Kennedy was born on November
20, 1925, in Brookline, Massachusetts, the

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:36.590
third boy and seventh out of a total of nine
children born to Rose and patriarch Joseph

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:37.590
P. Kennedy.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:42.269
Smaller and weaker than his older brothers
Joe Jr And John, Bobby was often considered

00:03:42.269 --> 00:03:46.290
the “runt” of the family, which meant
that at least in his early childhood he was

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:51.660
much attached to his devout mother, spending
much of his time going to church with her.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:56.209
But despite having a sweet and pleasant character
he showed early on a disposition to fight

00:03:56.209 --> 00:03:59.269
against the odds and to let his own voice
be heard.

00:03:59.269 --> 00:04:04.829
"I was the seventh of nine children, and when
you come from that far down you have to struggle

00:04:04.829 --> 00:04:06.019
to survive."

00:04:06.019 --> 00:04:09.660
Robert - or Bobby, as he was known to his
family – struggled not only at home, but

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:10.660
also at school.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:15.250
Due to Joseph Sr’s work-related relocations,
including an appointment as Ambassador to

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:18.570
London, Bobby had a hard time in adjusting
to different schools.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:24.030
He eventually attended 12 different primary
and secondary schools in the U.S. and England.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:28.750
But he pulled through, graduating from Milton
Academy and later at Harvard, where he proved

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:33.740
his mettle as an accomplished varsity football
player, despite him being a “runt” and

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:35.490
playing with a severely broken leg.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:40.770
In 1944, aged 19, Bobby interrupted his studies
to serve in the US Navy, being commissioned

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:46.020
to a relatively quiet theatre – the Caribbean
– on anti U-Boot patrolling duties.

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:50.050
The ship he served on was named after his
older brother Joseph P. Kennedy, Jr who had

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:53.270
been killed in action during the war as a
Navy fighter pilot.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:57.310
This tragedy had suddenly shifted the balance
of expectations among the Kennedy boys.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:02.500
Now, ‘Jack’ was suddenly pushed to the
fore, and Bobby was to be considered a close

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:03.620
‘second in command’.

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:08.870
In 1945, with WWII over, Bobby was able to
pursue more pleasing interests and he was

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:14.470
dating Patricia Skakel, the daughter of a
railroad clerk turned coal magnate.

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:17.919
Until he met and fell in love with one of
his sister Jean’s best friends, a younger

00:05:17.919 --> 00:05:19.340
girl called Ethel.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:22.040
Who happened to be Patricia’s sister.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:27.840
We have no records, but we are going to guess
Christmas 1945 must have been a pretty awkward

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:32.080
one at the Skakels’ …
But Bobby and Ethel made a nice couple, had

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:37.300
common interests and even worked together
on Jack’s campaign for the Congress in 1946.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:41.919
This was the first of many occasions in which
the future President would rely on Bobby’s

00:05:41.919 --> 00:05:43.949
trusted advice and support.

00:05:43.949 --> 00:05:48.750
In the meanwhile, Bobby returned to his studies
and earned a degree in government from Harvard

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:50.699
University in 1948.

00:05:50.699 --> 00:05:55.220
He completed his education by attaining also
a law degree from the University of Virginia

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:56.220
three years later.

00:05:56.220 --> 00:06:00.430
But, as he recalled on many occasions, he
considered his most formative experiences

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:05.560
to be the conversations at the family dinner
table, where Rose and Joe Sr would encourage

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:10.340
their children to engage in heated discussions
about history and current affairs.

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:13.980
In June 1950, after a brief engagement, Bobby
and Ethel got married.

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:19.280
Their first child, Kathleen, was born in 1951,
on the 4th of July – it doesn’t get more

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:20.789
patriotic than that.

00:06:20.789 --> 00:06:24.219
Kathleen would be the first of eleven – yes,
eleven – children.

00:06:24.219 --> 00:06:29.509
In 1952, Bobby made his formal debut on the
political stage, by managing his brother John's

00:06:29.509 --> 00:06:33.319
campaign to be elected as a Senator for the
State of Massachusetts.

00:06:33.319 --> 00:06:38.719
The campaign was successful and proved that
Bobby had a natural talent to organise and

00:06:38.719 --> 00:06:39.719
to lead.

00:06:39.719 --> 00:06:43.789
But the young Kennedy possessed another talent
which would come to the fore in the following

00:06:43.789 --> 00:06:49.620
year: he was in fact a skilful investigator
and prosecutor, and in 1953 he served briefly

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:56.091
on the Senate Subcommittee on Investigations,
chaired by Senator Joseph McCarthy.

00:06:56.091 --> 00:07:01.909
McCarthy was an old family friend – he had
even dated two of the Kennedy girls – and

00:07:01.909 --> 00:07:06.070
had hired Bobby to help him on his crackdown
on suspected communist infiltrators.

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:11.520
Bobby, however, did not agree with McCarthy’s
brutal prosecution tactics and left the Subcommittee

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:12.889
after only six months.

00:07:12.889 --> 00:07:17.389
He would later author a report condemning
McCarthy's investigation of alleged Communists

00:07:17.389 --> 00:07:18.389
in the Army.

00:07:18.389 --> 00:07:22.669
Bobby did not stop working within the Senate’s
investigating committees.

00:07:22.669 --> 00:07:26.419
By the end of the 1950s he had become Chief
Counsel for the Senate Rackets Committee,

00:07:26.419 --> 00:07:29.360
in charge of investigating corruption in trade
unions.

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:33.590
This position won him national recognition,
particularly because it pitted him directly

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:38.870
against the powerful Jimmy Hoffa, president
of the Brotherhood of Teamsters, the largest

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:39.900
truckers’ union.

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:45.620
Hoffa was suspected of colluding with organised
crime to further the progress and influence

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:50.259
of the Brotherhood and developed a bitter
personal feud with Kennedy, which became apparent

00:07:50.259 --> 00:07:52.540
in some of the televised Committee hearings.

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:58.370
Hoffa would later say of Bobby:
“I used to love to bug the little bastard”

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:06.169
Attorney General
In 1960, Bobby resigned from his Chief Counsel

00:08:06.169 --> 00:08:10.400
position to better dedicate himself to running
John F. Kennedy's presidential campaign.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:14.779
It was in this occasion that Bobby became
John’s closest confidante and collaborator.

00:08:14.779 --> 00:08:19.259
In fact, after being elected to the top office,
John appointed Bobby Attorney General in his

00:08:19.259 --> 00:08:20.259
cabinet.

00:08:20.259 --> 00:08:24.770
As Attorney General, Bobby gained a reputation
as the President’s loyal and ruthless enforcer

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:30.139
and some of his actions are still controversial,
but overall, he won respect for his effective

00:08:30.139 --> 00:08:32.760
administration of the Department of Justice.

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:35.930
Today he is mostly remembered for two endeavours.

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:38.720
First, his fight against organized crime.

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:43.830
According to author Seymour Hersh, Joseph
Kennedy had enlisted the help of mobster Sam

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:47.340
Giancana to support JFK’s presidential campaign.

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:51.440
But neither Jack nor Bobby had any interest
in maintaining this relationship.

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:58.779
When Bobby increased the number of Mafia convictions
from 35 to 288 over the three years of Jack’s

00:08:58.779 --> 00:09:00.860
term, the mob were furious.

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:04.180
According to Prof Larry Sabato it took the
good offices of Frank Sinatra – good friends

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:09.110
with both the Kennedys and the Mafia – to
appease Giancana: the crooner had to perform

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:11.750
eight nights for free at Giancana’s club.

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:17.250
Bobby’s second achievement was the enforcement
of the 1954 Supreme Court decision on school

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:22.250
desegregation, and in general his support
of the Civil Rights movement.

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:26.550
In September 1962, Attorney General Kennedy
sent US Marshals and troops to Oxford, Mississippi

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:31.180
to enforce a federal court order admitting
the first African American student - James

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:33.610
Meredith - to the University of Mississippi.

00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:37.690
He also collaborated with the President in
proposing the most far-reaching civil rights

00:09:37.690 --> 00:09:42.980
statute so far in American history, the Civil
Rights Act of 1964, which passed eight months

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:44.550
after JFK's death.

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:49.160
Bobby’s collaboration with his President
brother was not limited to Justice.

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:54.020
During the September 1962 Cuban Missile Crisis,
for example, he developed the strategy of

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:59.120
blockading Cuba as an alternative to military
intervention that could have led to nuclear

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:00.120
war.

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:04.180
But Cuba also marks one of the shadows in
the Attorney General’s career.

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:08.120
After the failure of the Bay of Pigs invasion
– a plan to overthrow Fidel Castro using

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:13.590
an ill-prepared force of Cuban exiles - President
Kennedy asked his brother to oversee a clandestine

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:19.390
mission, Operation Mongoose, dedicated to
removing the Cuban leader once and for all.

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:24.670
Bobby invested hundreds of millions of dollars
in building secret bases, training spies and

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:29.220
planning increasingly bizarre ways to do away
with Castro for good.

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:33.310
Operation Mongoose is known to have made at
least eight failed attempts on the Communist

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:39.020
leader’s life, one of which involved CIA
operatives hiring a Mafia hitman, Johnny Rosselli.

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:43.090
Considering Bobby’s stance against organised
crime, this further involvement with the mob

00:10:43.090 --> 00:10:45.980
is controversial to say the least.

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:49.390
Another controversial decision involved the
Civil Rights movement.

00:10:49.390 --> 00:10:53.740
Despite the Attorney General’s sympathies
towards this movement, in 1963 he approved

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:58.290
the installation of wiretaps on Martin Luther
King and several of his associates.

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:03.440
In this case Bobby relented to lobbying from
FBI director J Edgar Hoover who believed Dr

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:07.790
King to be a Communist sympathizer, mainly
because he had spoken up against the Vietnam

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:08.790
War.

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:13.450
For more than three years the Bureau would
keep King under surveillance and even sent

00:11:13.450 --> 00:11:23.310
him anonymous threatening letters in the hopes
of stopping his social justice campaigns.

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:31.770
Senator
On the 22nd of November 1963 John F. Kennedy

00:11:31.770 --> 00:11:37.220
was shot in Dallas and we invite you to watch
our video on JFK to learn more about the facts

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:39.040
and theories behind that killing.

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:44.970
Let’s not lose our focus on Bobby: John’s
death was a devastating blow for him.

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:49.720
Not only he had lost a brother whom he loved
dearly, but his years as campaign manager

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:54.640
and Attorney General had given him an identity,
which was now struggling to find.

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:58.410
He continued his duties at the Department
of Justice under Lyndon Johnson’s presidency

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:03.400
until 1964, but the two never got along well
and Bobby quit his job.

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:07.180
Instead he ran for the post of US Senator
for the State of New York, launching an effective

00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:13.160
campaign which won him the November election
by 719,000 votes.

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:17.140
As New York's Senator from January 1965, Bobby
dedicated himself to three main causes:

00:12:17.140 --> 00:12:23.190
First, he strived to supporting the dispossessed
and the powerless in America, mainly the urban

00:12:23.190 --> 00:12:26.890
poor populations, the racial minorities and
Native Americans.

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:31.020
He sought to remedy the problems of poverty
through legislation to encourage private industry

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:36.700
to locate in poverty-stricken areas, thus
creating jobs for the unemployed, and stressed

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:39.160
the importance of work over welfare.

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:43.420
Then, he sought to advance human rights, both
in the US and abroad.

00:12:43.420 --> 00:12:47.200
He was an outspoken critic of the apartheid
system in South Africa, visiting the country

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:52.420
in 1966 and delivering a memorable speech
to an assembly of progressive students

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:57.870
"Each time a man stands up for an ideal, or
acts to improve the lot of others, or strikes

00:12:57.870 --> 00:13:03.770
out against injustice, he sends forth a tiny
ripple of hope, and crossing each other from

00:13:03.770 --> 00:13:11.890
a million different centres of energy and
daring, those ripples build a current

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:17.180
And finally, he embarked on a personal quest
to end the Vietnam War.

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:21.820
Bobby had initially supported President Johnson’s
military escalation in Indochina - until February

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:23.290
1966.

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:27.200
This is when he first publicly denounced this
policy and asked for the reduction of the

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:30.970
war effort, as well as for the initiation
of talks with the Viet Cong and the North

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:32.020
Vietnamese government.

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:35.590
He strongly opposed President Johnson’s
authorisation of the carpet bombing of civilian

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:40.870
targets in North Vietnam, which he denounced
in another memorable speech in the Senate:

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:45.970
"Are we like the God of the Old Testament
that we can decide, in Washington, DC, what

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:49.540
cities, what towns, what hamlets in Vietnam
are going to be destroyed?...

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:51.200
Do we have to accept that?...

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:52.540
I do not think we have to.

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:56.310
I think we can do something about it."

00:13:56.310 --> 00:14:05.570
‘Everything is going to be OK’
On March 16, 1968, Robert Kennedy announced

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:09.040
his candidacy for the Democratic presidential
nomination.

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:13.460
He would be running on a very progressive
platform against the other main Democratic

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:15.010
candidate, Hubert Humphrey.

00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:17.880
It was, in the words of author Arthur Schlesinger
Jr.,

00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:21.510
"an uproarious campaign, filled with enthusiasm
and fun...

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:24.880
It was also a campaign moving in its sweep
and passion."

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:29.500
In his campaign Bobby built on the themes
that had marked his senatorial term: advancement

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:33.690
of human rights, including supporting the
Civil Rights movement, helping the dispossessed

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:38.920
in the urban areas and the Native American
reservations and putting an end to the Vietnam

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:39.920
War.

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:44.160
His candidates were supportive of a broader,
safer, more conservative message, and yet

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:49.010
Bobby managed to win critical primary elections
in Nebraska and Indiana.

00:14:49.010 --> 00:14:53.930
And it was just before speaking at an Indianapolis
rally that Bobby learned of the murder of

00:14:53.930 --> 00:14:55.420
Martin Luther King.

00:14:55.420 --> 00:15:01.080
It was the 4th of April 1968, five years since
the former Attorney General had approved of

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:03.640
the Reverend’s surveillance by the FBI.

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:07.720
That evening Bobby delivered one his most
famous speeches informing the crowd of King’s

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:10.600
death and urging them to not react angrily.

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:14.890
He concluded by making an appeal for racial
unity in those difficult times.

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:19.990
Following King’s death, riots broke out
in more than 100 cities across the US, but

00:15:19.990 --> 00:15:22.330
Indianapolis remained peaceful.

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:26.720
After securing Nebraska and Indiana, Bobby
was looking forward to winning the California

00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:27.840
primaries in early June.

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:30.820
The Democratic candidacy was within his grasp.

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:33.720
And so, we are back to the start of our video.

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:39.750
It’s the night between the 4th and the 5th
of June 1968, Ambassador Hotel, Los Angeles.

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:44.260
Robert F. Kennedy has just announced his victory
at the California primaries to an ecstatic

00:15:44.260 --> 00:15:45.590
crowd of supporters.

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:48.490
After a brief speech Bobby mingled with the
crowd and Hotel staff.

00:15:48.490 --> 00:15:52.730
According to witnesses, he was moving slowly
through the Hotel restaurant’s pantry.

00:15:52.730 --> 00:15:56.550
When he reached out to shake the hand of a
busboy, Juan Romero, a young man stepped out

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:21.880
shooting.

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:27.050
That man was called Sirhan Sirhan, a 24-year
old Palestinian refugee.

00:16:27.050 --> 00:16:31.620
Kennedy was hit three times: in his armpit,
in the back and behind his right ear.

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:36.470
Members of his entourage apprehended Sirhan
and slammed him down on a metal table, but

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:40.000
he was able to continue shooting, wounding
five other by-standers.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:43.650
As Kennedy’s friends, which included a professional
Football player, struggled to pin down the

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:46.230
diminutive Sirhan, he yelled
"Let me explain!

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:47.390
I can explain!

00:16:47.390 --> 00:16:49.620
I did it for my country.

00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:51.470
I love my country."

00:16:51.470 --> 00:16:54.540
Juan Romero knelt to help Bobby, who was on
the floor, bleeding.

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:57.090
Kennedy asked
"Is everybody OK?”

00:16:57.090 --> 00:16:59.930
Romero replied that 'Yes, everybody's OK'.

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:04.410
Bobby then turned away and said
“Everything's going to be OK.”

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:06.059
Those were his last words.

00:17:06.059 --> 00:17:10.040
Robert Kennedy died 26 hours later, aged 42.

00:17:10.040 --> 00:17:14.540
His eleventh child, Rory, would be born six
months later.

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:19.500
Act II
Sirhan

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:24.670
It’s time now to examine the life of the
man on the other side of the gun.

00:17:24.670 --> 00:17:29.100
Who was Sirhan Sirhan and what had driven
him to murder Robert Kennedy?

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:36.040
Sirhan Bishara Sirhan was a Jordanian citizen
born on March 19, 1944, in Jerusalem, Mandatory

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:39.380
Palestine, into a highly religious family
of Arab–Christians.

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:44.179
He spent the early few years of his life in
his home country and also completed his early

00:17:44.179 --> 00:17:45.179
schooling there.

00:17:45.179 --> 00:17:49.691
If you know even a little of Middle Eastern
history, you may have guessed that being a

00:17:49.691 --> 00:17:55.250
Palestinian child in the late 1940s did not
make for a quiet upbringing, and Sirhan’s

00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:57.220
childhood was no exception.

00:17:57.220 --> 00:18:01.610
Following the declaration of Israel as an
independent state and the subsequent declaration

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:06.400
of war by the surrounding Arab Countries,
Sirhan and his family would witness violence

00:18:06.400 --> 00:18:08.169
on a daily basis.

00:18:08.169 --> 00:18:12.510
In one traumatic experience, Sirhan saw a
man being ripped to pieces during a bombing

00:18:12.510 --> 00:18:14.030
raid in his neighbourhood.

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:18.429
His mother, Mary, said that the image haunted
her son, and he would never be the same.

00:18:18.429 --> 00:18:23.320
At the age of 12, the Sirhans had the chance
to emigrate to the United States, as part

00:18:23.320 --> 00:18:26.669
of a special visa programme granted to Palestinian
refugees.

00:18:26.669 --> 00:18:30.510
The young Sirhan did not escape completely
from a life of violence, though, as his father

00:18:30.510 --> 00:18:35.710
had a volatile temper and would physically
assault him on several occasions.

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:42.490
Life in America
Despite being an outsider within a dysfunctional

00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:45.210
family, Sirhan adapted quite well to American
life.

00:18:45.210 --> 00:18:49.850
He first attended the Eliot Junior High School
in New York, before the family relocated to

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:53.390
California where he enrolled in the Pasadena
City College.

00:18:53.390 --> 00:18:57.519
Sirhan was academically good and proved his
worth in both school and college.

00:18:57.519 --> 00:19:02.240
However, despite having the chance to do so,
he never applied for American citizenship

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:04.919
and preferred to remain a Jordanian.

00:19:04.919 --> 00:19:09.950
After graduating from Pasadena, Sirhan drifted
from one job to another, never settling into

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:13.259
a career and holding a series of menial jobs.

00:19:13.259 --> 00:19:17.389
The only career prospect he considered seriously
was horse racing.

00:19:17.389 --> 00:19:22.350
At one point, he found himself working as
a stable boy at the Santa Anita racetrack.

00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:27.590
Being only 5 feet 5 inches tall and weighing
115 pounds, he had the perfect physique to

00:19:27.590 --> 00:19:31.470
become a professional jockey, but his hopes
did not materialise.

00:19:31.470 --> 00:19:35.860
What did really define him at this stage in
his life was his religious belief.

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:39.990
He was an ardent Christian believer and he
experimented with different church denominations,

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:45.059
shifting from being a Coptic to joining the
Baptist and the Adventist churches.

00:19:45.059 --> 00:19:49.880
In 1966, he finally joined the ‘Ancient
Mystical Order of the Rose Cross,’ an American

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:51.779
branch of Rosicrucianism.

00:19:51.779 --> 00:19:55.980
This is a mystical branch of Christianity
which dates back to the teachings of Johan

00:19:55.980 --> 00:20:01.110
Valentin Andreae, a XVIIth century Lutheran
theologian.

00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:06.909
Rosicrucians combined early Christian philosophy
with alchemy and even ancient Egyptian mysticism

00:20:06.909 --> 00:20:11.279
and have been associated with Freemasonry
and Theosophism through the ages.

00:20:11.279 --> 00:20:15.950
We could talk about Rosicrucianism for hours
on an end, but for the purpose of our story

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:21.179
we will only mention that Sirhan’s association
to this movement has been linked to his shift

00:20:21.179 --> 00:20:26.630
towards religious extremism, nationalism or
even brainwashing.

00:20:26.630 --> 00:20:33.950
Sirhan and Bobby
So what we have so far is a deeply religious

00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:39.000
yet alienated young man, with few prospects
in life and a violent upbringing.

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:41.570
Was this enough to push him towards murder?

00:20:41.570 --> 00:20:43.750
And why Bobby Kennedy?

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:46.370
What was his relationship with him?

00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:50.780
Sirhan would declare to journalist David Frost
that he saw Robert Kennedy as a hero, a protector

00:20:50.780 --> 00:20:56.450
of the downtrodden and the disadvantaged
‘ … and I felt that I was one of those’

00:20:56.450 --> 00:21:01.980
But this perception changed in June 1967 with
the six-day war, another victory which the

00:21:01.980 --> 00:21:04.900
State of Israel had gained against its Arab
neighbours.

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:09.080
As a Senator, Robert Kennedy had openly supported
Israel during that conflict.

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:13.830
After announcing his candidacy in March 1968
as new Democratic hopeful President, Kennedy

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:16.710
made his support of Israel more frequent and
outspoken.

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:22.230
At a speech in a synagogue, broadcasted via
radio, Kennedy pledged to support Israel with

00:21:22.230 --> 00:21:24.409
50 fighter jets should he become President.

00:21:24.409 --> 00:21:29.509
Sirhan’s feelings towards the candidate
had grown increasingly hostile since the Six-day

00:21:29.509 --> 00:21:30.509
war.

00:21:30.509 --> 00:21:34.499
After hearing the speech, Sirhan had a violent
reaction witnessed by his family, screaming

00:21:34.499 --> 00:21:36.529
and storming out of the room.

00:21:36.529 --> 00:21:41.149
On the 18th of May, Sirhan wrote in his diary:
"My determination to eliminate R.F.K. is becoming

00:21:41.149 --> 00:21:48.279
the more and more of an unshakable obsession...Kennedy
must die before June 5th … die, die, die,

00:21:48.279 --> 00:21:49.549
die, die.”

00:21:49.549 --> 00:21:54.179
The 5th of June 1968, it would have been the
first anniversary of the Six-days War.

00:21:54.179 --> 00:21:57.820
On the 1st of June, witnesses reported seeing
Sirhan at the Lock, Stock, ‘N Barrel gun

00:21:57.820 --> 00:22:02.960
shop in Los Angeles, where he bought two boxes
of .22-caliber hollow point bullets.

00:22:02.960 --> 00:22:06.869
On the 3rd of June, he was first spotted by
staff at the Ambassador Hotel, apparently

00:22:06.869 --> 00:22:11.049
surveying the site where the presidential
hopeful would be expected to wait for the

00:22:11.049 --> 00:22:14.259
results of the California primaries on the
following day.

00:22:14.259 --> 00:22:18.650
On the 4th of June, only hours before the
shooting, Sirhan visited the San Gabriel Valley

00:22:18.650 --> 00:22:21.400
Gun Club to practice at its gun range.

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:24.230
And now to the night of the 4th, a few minutes
before midnight.

00:22:24.230 --> 00:22:27.841
Robert Kennedy was delivering the last lines
of his speech in the Embassy ballroom at the

00:22:27.841 --> 00:22:33.240
Ambassador hotel, while Sirhan was in the
hotel’s kitchen pantry area, waiting - with

00:22:33.240 --> 00:22:36.559
a .22-caliber Iver-Johnson Cadet handgun in
his pocket.

00:22:36.559 --> 00:22:41.740
Ambassador employees Jesus Perez and Martin
Petrusky, remembered Sirhan lingering around

00:22:41.740 --> 00:22:45.860
the elevator area as Kennedy was still on
stage.

00:22:45.860 --> 00:22:49.549
You know what happened next: the screams,
the gun shots, Kennedy falling on the floor,

00:22:49.549 --> 00:22:59.670
while Sirhan was apprehended still yelling
“I did it for my country!”.

00:22:59.670 --> 00:23:05.789
After the arrest
Sirhan initially refused to speak or identify

00:23:05.789 --> 00:23:06.919
himself to the police.

00:23:06.919 --> 00:23:10.590
It wasn’t until the 9th of June that decided
to confess to the crime.

00:23:10.590 --> 00:23:14.450
But on insistence from his lawyers, he retracted
his confession and pleaded not guilty.

00:23:14.450 --> 00:23:20.140
The trial took place between January and April
1969 and during court hearings Sirhan behaved

00:23:20.140 --> 00:23:21.159
erratically.

00:23:21.159 --> 00:23:25.070
Sometimes he claimed that on the night of
the murder he was drunk and that he had no

00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:29.350
recollection of killing Kennedy, while in
other occasions he stated that if he had killed

00:23:29.350 --> 00:23:37.230
him, it wasn’t out of personal hatred but
as an act in service to his Country, Palestine.

00:23:37.230 --> 00:23:41.299
These discrepancies may have been part of
the defence strategy, based on the concept

00:23:41.299 --> 00:23:44.919
that Sirhan was suffering from a condition
known as ‘diminished capacity’, a thesis

00:23:44.919 --> 00:23:46.029
supported by professor of psychiatry at UCLA,
Bernard Diamond.

00:23:46.029 --> 00:23:50.820
The jury was not convinced, though, and eventually
Sirhan was found guilty of murder on the 17th

00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:54.159
of April 1969 and sentenced to death.

00:23:54.159 --> 00:23:59.820
His story may have ended there, but in 1972
the State of California declared the death

00:23:59.820 --> 00:24:05.330
penalty to be unconstitutional and so his
sentence was commuted to life imprisonment.

00:24:05.330 --> 00:24:09.879
Sirhan Sirhan has been a convict in the Californian
state prisons since then, first serving time

00:24:09.879 --> 00:24:14.490
in San Quentin, then Soledad, Pleasant Valley
and finally the Richard Donovan Correctional

00:24:14.490 --> 00:24:16.159
Facility in San Diego.

00:24:16.159 --> 00:24:20.500
Over the years Sirhan has not been a silent
convict, far from it.

00:24:20.500 --> 00:24:24.499
His lawyers have been constantly filing requests
for parole hearings: one of these is held

00:24:24.499 --> 00:24:29.019
every five years, the last one in 2016, and
they have all been rejected.

00:24:29.019 --> 00:24:31.990
What is interesting about these hearings,
though, is that they have given the chance

00:24:31.990 --> 00:24:36.929
to Sirhan, his lawyers and his supporters
to present new evidence supporting the claim

00:24:36.929 --> 00:24:41.780
that he was not Kennedy’s assassin – or
at least not a willing one – or maybe not

00:24:41.780 --> 00:24:42.780
the only one.

00:24:42.780 --> 00:24:44.379
It's time now to look at these theories.

00:24:44.379 --> 00:24:46.900
I hope you are not easily offended by the
‘C- word’: Conspiracy.

00:24:46.900 --> 00:24:57.200
Act III
The Conspiracy

00:24:57.200 --> 00:25:01.149
The official explanation for the murder of
Robert F. Kennedy is that Sirhan Sirhan had

00:25:01.149 --> 00:25:06.179
acted alone, because he was mentally instable,
because he wanted to strike at an enemy of

00:25:06.179 --> 00:25:08.470
the Arab cause, or both.

00:25:08.470 --> 00:25:12.029
This would make Bobby’s assassination the
first American encounter with Middle Eastern

00:25:12.029 --> 00:25:13.049
terrorism.

00:25:13.049 --> 00:25:17.080
Over the years many more theories have emerged,
claiming that Sirhan had not acted alone or

00:25:17.080 --> 00:25:25.260
that he had been a pawn in the hands of more
powerful and sinister forces.

00:25:25.260 --> 00:25:31.570
Hypnosis
At the 2011 parole hearing, Sirhan’s attorney

00:25:31.570 --> 00:25:36.720
Larry Teeter brought forward the hypothesis
that Sirhan may have been hypnotised, brainwashed

00:25:36.720 --> 00:25:40.200
and conditioned to carry out the assassination
of RFK.

00:25:40.200 --> 00:25:44.419
He had been identified and selected as a ‘patsy’
or ‘fall guy’, because of his foreign

00:25:44.419 --> 00:25:47.289
origin and support of the Palestinian cause.

00:25:47.289 --> 00:25:51.950
These theory is supported also by British
author Peter Evans in his book Nemesis.

00:25:51.950 --> 00:25:56.620
According to Evans and Teeter, after interrogating
Sirhan the Los Angeles Police Department could

00:25:56.620 --> 00:26:01.509
not account for a period of three months,
known as the “white fog”, during which

00:26:01.509 --> 00:26:02.929
Sirhan’s movements were unknown.

00:26:02.929 --> 00:26:07.289
It was during this ‘white fog’ days that
Sirhan may have been hypnotised by psychiatrist

00:26:07.289 --> 00:26:13.369
Dr William Joseph Bryan Jnr, who had worked
on the infamous CIA mind-control programme

00:26:13.369 --> 00:26:14.940
called MKULTRA.

00:26:14.940 --> 00:26:19.919
This programme was an expansion on two pre-existing
operations run by the CIA in the 1950s, called

00:26:19.919 --> 00:26:22.700
Project Bluebird and Project Artichoke.

00:26:22.700 --> 00:26:27.629
Both projects envisage the possibility of
using hypnosis as an interrogation technique

00:26:27.629 --> 00:26:32.059
or as a way of manipulating a foreign national
– and I stress, a foreign national - to

00:26:32.059 --> 00:26:34.470
carry out political assassinations.

00:26:34.470 --> 00:26:39.600
Bluebird, Artichoke and MKULTRA, as outlandish
as they may sound, have all been acknowledged

00:26:39.600 --> 00:26:44.320
by the CIA and documentation related to them
is freely accessible via Freedom of Information

00:26:44.320 --> 00:26:45.320
requests.

00:26:45.320 --> 00:26:49.919
What is chilling is that the official documentation
for Bluebird and Artichoke does not raise

00:26:49.919 --> 00:26:55.600
any moral considerations around using hypnosis
in interrogations or brainwashing innocent

00:26:55.600 --> 00:26:58.169
people to turn them into assassins.

00:26:58.169 --> 00:27:03.239
The main concern is sourcing the right psychiatrist
for the job, because a private practitioner

00:27:03.239 --> 00:27:06.870
would likely not accept a lowly CIA salary
...

00:27:06.870 --> 00:27:10.070
Didn’t know that the ‘C’ in CIA stood
for ‘Cheap’ (!)

00:27:10.070 --> 00:27:12.600
But back to the 2011 parole hearing!

00:27:12.600 --> 00:27:15.239
Why did the hypnosis theory emerge only then?

00:27:15.239 --> 00:27:18.990
Well, ironically enough, it was only then
that Attorney Teeter had the idea to have

00:27:18.990 --> 00:27:23.700
Sirhan hypnotised to retrieve repressed memories
of the assassination.

00:27:23.700 --> 00:27:28.139
During those sessions Sirhan was able to remember
a detail previously concealed.

00:27:28.139 --> 00:27:32.369
He remembered meeting a girl in a polka-dot
dress on the night of the assassination

00:27:32.369 --> 00:27:35.919
"I was fascinated with her looks .... She
never said much.

00:27:35.919 --> 00:27:37.029
It was very erotic.

00:27:37.029 --> 00:27:39.149
I was consumed by her.

00:27:39.149 --> 00:27:42.960
She was a seductress with an unspoken unavailability."

00:27:42.960 --> 00:27:46.369
The girl took him to the kitchen pantry and
then pinched him on the arm.

00:27:46.369 --> 00:27:50.529
This was a ‘trigger action’ which led
him to believe that he was on a weapons firing

00:27:50.529 --> 00:27:52.999
range – that’s when Sirhan began shooting.

00:27:52.999 --> 00:27:56.080
But who were the brains behind the whole operation?

00:27:56.080 --> 00:27:59.789
According to Teeter,
"The assassination was staged by US intelligence

00:27:59.789 --> 00:28:04.509
for the purpose of continuing the war against
Vietnam and putting the Republican Party in

00:28:04.509 --> 00:28:05.509
the White House.

00:28:05.509 --> 00:28:10.289
The assassination was arranged with the CIA,
the FBI and the LAPD.

00:28:10.289 --> 00:28:12.350
There was a massive cover-up.

00:28:12.350 --> 00:28:17.369
If he had lived and been allowed to run, Bobby
Kennedy would have been elected president

00:28:17.369 --> 00:28:21.239
and this was a multi-agency task force to
make sure that the Democrats didn't take the

00:28:21.239 --> 00:28:22.379
White House again."

00:28:22.379 --> 00:28:26.940
On the other hand, Peter Evans states a completely
different theory in Nemesis.

00:28:26.940 --> 00:28:31.370
Sirhan had been hypnotised to be at the Ambassador
and take the blame off the actual assassin,

00:28:31.370 --> 00:28:34.240
a Palestinian terrorist named Mahmoud Hamshari.

00:28:34.240 --> 00:28:39.809
And Hamshari was himself a pawn, on the payroll
of none other than Greek magnate Aristotle

00:28:39.809 --> 00:28:44.370
Onassis, Jackie Kennedy’s suitor at that
time.

00:28:44.370 --> 00:28:45.739
The motive?

00:28:45.739 --> 00:28:49.710
Personal resentment towards Bobby, who had
foiled a major deal between Onassis and the

00:28:49.710 --> 00:28:54.850
Saudis in 1953 and was opposed to the Greek
billionaire marrying his sister-in-law.

00:28:54.850 --> 00:28:59.870
According to Evans, the CIA psychiatrist Dr
Bryan had links to both Hamshari and Onassis,

00:28:59.870 --> 00:29:03.889
having cured the former for migraine, and
the latter for sexual dysfunction.

00:29:03.889 --> 00:29:08.350
And finally one of Onassis’ lovers, Helen
Gaillet De Neergaard, reported that he himself

00:29:08.350 --> 00:29:10.990
had admitted his complicity in the killing
in1974.

00:29:10.990 --> 00:29:13.320
Oh, by the way, Dr Bryan?

00:29:13.320 --> 00:29:18.480
He was found dead in a Las Vegas hotel room
in 1978, either shot himself or was murdered.

00:29:18.480 --> 00:29:21.070
The case remains unsolved.

00:29:21.070 --> 00:29:25.790
The brainwashing theory is certainly fascinating,
and we know by the CIA’s own admission that

00:29:25.790 --> 00:29:29.850
the use of hypnosis to interrogate, or kill,
was in their plans.

00:29:29.850 --> 00:29:34.700
But something does not add up, and please
note these are our personal considerations:

00:29:34.700 --> 00:29:38.869
if Sirhan had been programmed to believe he
was at a firing range, shooting at targets

00:29:38.869 --> 00:29:43.059
if such belief was triggered by the pinch
from the girl in the polka-dot dress

00:29:43.059 --> 00:29:46.690
why did he shout, “Kennedy you son of a
bitch?”.

00:29:46.690 --> 00:29:49.100
Why did he shout, “I did it for my country?”

00:29:49.100 --> 00:29:54.279
If he was a ‘patsy’ all along, acting
mechanically at the tap of some girl in polka-dots,

00:29:54.279 --> 00:29:57.260
how could he behave in such a competent way
prior to the assassination?

00:29:57.260 --> 00:30:01.769
He knew where Kennedy was due to speak, he
visited the location, he practised at a firing

00:30:01.769 --> 00:30:07.409
range and he acquired a .22 caliber gun – a
low powered pistol, perfect choice for shooting

00:30:07.409 --> 00:30:09.320
in a closed environment such a pantry.

00:30:09.320 --> 00:30:14.370
Now, this choice of a weapon makes even more
sense if other assassins are there.

00:30:14.370 --> 00:30:20.009
Other hitmen, even more competent, who want
to avoid the risk of being hit by ‘friendly

00:30:20.009 --> 00:30:21.009
fire’.

00:30:21.009 --> 00:30:24.490
Time for our second Conspiracy theory.

00:30:24.490 --> 00:30:31.730
Multiple shooters
While researching the case for a screenplay,

00:30:31.730 --> 00:30:36.249
author and reporter Shane O’Sullivan uncovered
new video and photographic evidence suggesting

00:30:36.249 --> 00:30:39.600
that three senior CIA operatives were behind
the killing.

00:30:39.600 --> 00:30:45.519
This time, not as shady hypnotists, but as
hitmen involved directly in the assassination.

00:30:45.519 --> 00:30:50.580
The first agent is David Sanchez Morales,
known for leading covert operations in Latin

00:30:50.580 --> 00:30:51.580
America.

00:30:51.580 --> 00:30:54.419
As far back as 1973, Morales had been reported
as saying

00:30:54.419 --> 00:30:59.080
"I was in Dallas when we got the son of a
bitch and I was in Los Angeles when we got

00:30:59.080 --> 00:31:00.080
the little bastard."

00:31:00.080 --> 00:31:02.570
Referring to both Kennedy brothers, of course.

00:31:02.570 --> 00:31:06.740
Analysing footage and stills from the night
of the assassination, ‘O Sullivan was able

00:31:06.740 --> 00:31:11.450
to identify Morales standing at the back of
the ballroom, in the moments between the end

00:31:11.450 --> 00:31:13.320
of Kennedy's speech and the shooting.

00:31:13.320 --> 00:31:17.259
Morales was also spotted alongside another
operative called Gordon Campbell.

00:31:17.259 --> 00:31:21.320
Morales and Campbell had worked together at
the CIA’s Miami base in 1963.

00:31:21.320 --> 00:31:24.860
Both had been involved in the planning of
the Bay of the Pigs invasion and were harsh

00:31:24.860 --> 00:31:28.499
critics of the Kennedys, blaming them for
the failure of that operation.

00:31:28.499 --> 00:31:32.230
A third senior CIA figure was identified by
looking at the crime scene photos taken by

00:31:32.230 --> 00:31:39.700
the LAPD: George Joannides, chief of psychological
warfare operations at the Miami base.

00:31:39.700 --> 00:31:44.690
Whatever the involvement of Morales, Campbell
and Joannides, it is a shared belief that

00:31:44.690 --> 00:31:48.080
Sirhan was not the only shooter at the Ambassador
hotel.

00:31:48.080 --> 00:31:53.429
In the last parole hearing in 2016, Paul Schrade,
one of the five other people injured in the

00:31:53.429 --> 00:31:58.590
shooting, said the evidence clearly showed
a second gunman had been in the kitchen pantry.

00:31:58.590 --> 00:32:00.429
First piece of evidence, the number of shots.

00:32:00.429 --> 00:32:04.809
Sirhan’s gun could only carry eight rounds,
and yet a radio reporter recorded the sound

00:32:04.809 --> 00:32:07.320
of 13 shots being fired in the pantry.

00:32:07.320 --> 00:32:11.919
This was confirmed by campaign volunteer Nina
Rhodes-Hughes who reported to the FBI that

00:32:11.919 --> 00:32:14.830
she heard anywhere from 12-14 shots that night.

00:32:14.830 --> 00:32:19.739
Bobby’s own son, Robert Kennedy Jr is convinced
of this thesis, as he declared to The Washington

00:32:19.739 --> 00:32:21.919
Post:
“There were too many bullets.

00:32:21.919 --> 00:32:24.940
You can’t fire 13 shots out of an eight-shot
gun.”

00:32:24.940 --> 00:32:26.850
Second point: direction of shooting.

00:32:26.850 --> 00:32:31.570
How could Sirhan have shot Kennedy in the
back and behind the ear if all eye witnesses

00:32:31.570 --> 00:32:34.710
confirm that he was standing in front of him?

00:32:34.710 --> 00:32:35.750
Third: distance.

00:32:35.750 --> 00:32:39.950
Los Angeles County Coroner Thomas Noguchi
found that Bobby’s fatal head wound, with

00:32:39.950 --> 00:32:44.799
an entry trajectory form behind the ear, had
been inflicted from a distance of 1 inch to

00:32:44.799 --> 00:32:45.799
1 1/2 inches.

00:32:45.799 --> 00:32:49.149
And Sirhan, he had been standing at at least
18 inches’ distance.

00:32:49.149 --> 00:32:54.289
So, another hitman, closer to Bobby than Sirhan
was, had shot him behind the ear at close

00:32:54.289 --> 00:32:55.289
distance.

00:32:55.289 --> 00:32:56.289
Morales?

00:32:56.289 --> 00:32:57.289
Campbell?

00:32:57.289 --> 00:32:58.289
Joannides?

00:32:58.289 --> 00:32:59.350
Or somebody else?

00:32:59.350 --> 00:33:03.869
According to some witnesses, a security guard
called Thane Cesar, standing behind Kennedy

00:33:03.869 --> 00:33:06.309
at the time was seen drawing his weapon.

00:33:06.309 --> 00:33:10.480
Although we should specify, he was not seen
shooting and he later passed a polygraph test

00:33:10.480 --> 00:33:15.119
that included questions about whether he shot
Kennedy.

00:33:15.119 --> 00:33:23.619
Can we handle the truth?

00:33:23.619 --> 00:33:26.200
We have presented only three possible explanations
of who, why and how could have been behind

00:33:26.200 --> 00:33:30.320
the assassination of Robert Kennedy, Bobby,
a man who could have shone a beacon of hope

00:33:30.320 --> 00:33:32.970
in a traumatic period of American history.

00:33:32.970 --> 00:33:37.080
He could have ended the Vietnam War much earlier,
supported the cause of the desperately poor

00:33:37.080 --> 00:33:41.500
and accelerated the process of integration
brought about by the Civil Rights movement.

00:33:41.500 --> 00:33:46.159
These progressive goals would be at least
partially achieved by subsequent administrations.

00:33:46.159 --> 00:33:50.549
But sadly at that time they could have provided
enough motive for US intelligence agencies

00:33:50.549 --> 00:33:54.070
– or at least for factions within them – to
be involved in Bobby’s killing.

00:33:54.070 --> 00:33:56.570
And what was Sirhan’s real role in this
event?

00:33:56.570 --> 00:34:01.470
Was he really the victim of brainwashing,
or perhaps the willing participant of a larger

00:34:01.470 --> 00:34:04.110
conspiracy, the only one to take the blame?

00:34:04.110 --> 00:34:09.990
We will stand by to hear from Sirhan’s next
parole hearing in 2021, hoping that the truth

00:34:09.990 --> 00:34:11.490
will finally emerge.

00:34:11.490 --> 00:34:14.940
Whether we will be able to handle it, that’s
another question.

00:34:14.940 --> 00:34:21.190
So I hoped you liked this new, extended format,
please leave your comments as usual.

00:34:21.190 --> 00:34:22.190
Did you like it?

00:34:22.190 --> 00:34:23.190
Hate it?

00:34:23.190 --> 00:34:28.520
But most of all, don’t forget to tell us
what is your theory for Robert Kennedy’s

00:34:28.520 --> 00:34:29.520
assassination.

00:34:29.520 --> 00:34:41.490
And as usual, thank you 
for watching.

